# Line-ending policy.
#
# LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree on every platform. This is not cosmetic:
# `dotnet format` derives its expected line ending from .editorconfig, and when `end_of_line` is
# unset it falls back to the PLATFORM default — CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux. That made the
# formatter pass on a Windows checkout and fail inside the Linux build container on the exact same
# source, which with TreatWarningsAsErrors turns into a broken `docker build` that reproduces
# nowhere else. Pinning eol=lf here and `end_of_line = lf` in .editorconfig keeps the two agreeing.
#
# CRAFT runs on Linux; the .ps1 runtime scripts and the Dockerfile are all consumed there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never translate.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.br  binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary
